Tasks: dalogin persistence and Servlet adaptation

Feature
- `speckit.system.dalogin-servlet-request-response.specify`

Plan
- `speckit.system.dalogin-persistence-servlet-adaptation.plan`

Implementation model
- `speckit.system.dalogin-persistence-servlet-adaptation.implementation-example.md`

Phase 1 — Combined baseline (`@backend-dev`, `@testing-engineer`)
- [ ] Start from a clean, committed git state so the whole pass can be reverted as one unit if it
      does not land (the only revert path; no partial rollback is designed).
- [ ] Inventory all 14 Servlet mappings and methods.
- [ ] Account for all 26 `doGet`/`doPost` handlers.
- [ ] Inventory all 10 `init()`, all 10 `destroy()`, and relevant private flow helpers.
- [ ] Inventory every header, parameter, request attribute, and session input.
- [ ] Inventory every status, content type, encoding, JSON field/type, redirect, header, and cookie.
- [ ] Classify every request flow as complex, simple pass-through, or no-input, with a reason.
- [ ] Mark a DTO for each complex flow and every response-helper operation.
- [ ] Mark the final SQLAccess family beans each Servlet/filter/listener injects.
- [ ] Capture missing/malformed input outcomes before extraction.
- [ ] Record baseline SQL text and resource counts required by the SQLAccess features.

Phase 2 — Persistence foundation (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Complete datasource legacy removal without compiling.
- [x] Create final CDI-backed family beans directly.
- [x] Place each family in its own persistence subpackage with the domain naming agreed in
      `speckit.system.dalogin-sqlaccess-family-split.tasks` Phase 2.
- [ ] Move every SQLAccess method to its final family.
- [x] Apply explicit ResultSet closing and transaction cleanup required by CDI injection.
- [x] Add shared SQL support and cross-family connection-accepting forms.
- [ ] Preserve the registration procedure order.
- [x] Add atomic `DeviceSessionManager.establishLogin` for device/session/token creation.

Phase 3 — Servlet HTTP types (`@backend-dev`)
- [x] Add shared stateless `ServletResponses`.
- [x] Add injected stateless `CryptoService` with request-local cipher state.
- [ ] Migrate seven Servlet `AesUtil` fields and `ChangePswFilter` to `CryptoService`.
- [ ] Add immutable DTOs for every complex request-processing flow.
- [x] Implement every complex request DTO as a Java record.
- [x] Keep simple pass-through request reads explicit in their Servlet.
- [x] Do not add empty or ceremonial DTOs for simple/no-input flows.
- [x] Add endpoint-specific response helpers for all 14 Servlets.
- [ ] Share helpers only after proving wire contracts identical.
- [x] Keep all DTO/helper types outside persistence packages.

Phase 4 — Final caller migration (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Edit each Servlet once into its final shape.
- [ ] Refactor every declared GET and POST handler, not only the SQLAccess-calling path.
- [ ] Review and refactor each Servlet's private request/response/persistence helpers.
- [ ] Inject only final family beans.
- [x] Confirm no Servlet injects `DataSource` or acquires `Connection` directly.
- [x] Replace every static/context-bound SQLAccess call.
- [ ] Replace complex direct input parsing with DTO factories.
- [x] Preserve simple pass-through reads without introducing unnecessary models.
- [ ] Replace direct response construction with named helper operations.
- [ ] Migrate filters/listeners directly to final family beans.
- [ ] Preserve orchestration, session mutation, crypto, redirects, downstream clients, and logging.
- [ ] Preserve all endpoint wire behavior and SQL call order.
- [ ] In `HelloWorld` and `RegistrationWithoutVoucher`, create only a pending session before
      persistence and use atomic `establishLogin`.
- [ ] In `Registration`, keep `wrapUpRegistration` atomic and treat the session as pending until it
      commits.
- [ ] Publish session attributes only after the required transaction commits.
- [ ] Invalidate each pending session and return 5xx on persistence failure.
- [ ] Remove the `RegActivation` session created solely to obtain `ServletContext`.
- [ ] Remove the obsolete 100 ms token retry.

Phase 5 — Legacy deletion (`@backend-dev`)
- [x] Delete empty monolithic `SQLAccess`.
- [ ] Remove DBManager ServletContext publication and legacy fallback/dead manager code.
- [ ] Delete `SystemConstants.DB_CATALOG`/`extractCatalog()` (last readers gone) and the dead
      `DB_URL` env entries in `k8infra/quarkus-backend.yaml` and `k8infra/kubernetes.yaml`.
- [ ] Remove obsolete Servlet response builders, writers, imports, and parsing locals.
- [ ] Remove all ten Servlet `init()` and ten no-op `destroy()` overrides.
- [ ] Preserve key size, iteration count, salts, IVs, passphrases, and ciphertext format.
- [ ] Confirm no pass-through facade, compatibility overload, or temporary caller shape remains.
- [ ] Confirm no direct Servlet `JSONObject` construction or `PrintWriter` ownership remains.

Phase 6 — First build (`@backend-dev`)
- [x] Compile for the first time only after Phases 2-5 are complete.
- [ ] Treat compiler errors as the remaining migration list.
- [x] Resolve every caller, import, signature, and type error.
- [x] Confirm no legacy static SQLAccess or DBManager call shape survives.

Phase 7 — Automated verification (`@testing-engineer`)
- [ ] Run targeted `LoginFlowTest` with `.ai/skills/quarkus-local-test-mysql/SKILL.md`.
- [ ] Verify login success, bad HMAC, wrong password, and missing required input.
- [ ] Verify mobile/web JSON types, cookies, and `X-Token` response header.
- [ ] Verify malformed micro-time preserves its captured baseline outcome.
- [ ] Force a normal-login persistence failure and verify rollback, session invalidation, and 5xx.
- [ ] Confirm tests require neither `mbook`/`mbooks` nor Apache.

Phase 8 — Static and owner verification (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Diff all SQL text, parameter ordering, and result mapping.
- [ ] Confirm explicit connection/statement/ResultSet closure and rollback requirements.
- [ ] Confirm DTO coverage matches all and only flows classified complex.
- [ ] Confirm all response branches map to helpers with unchanged contracts.
- [ ] Confirm all 14 Servlet annotations are unchanged.
- [ ] Confirm all 26 request handlers and every declared lifecycle override were reviewed.
- [ ] Run concurrent crypto coverage; confirm no request-shared mutable `Cipher` remains.
- [ ] Hand registration, voucher, activation, password reset, logout, admin, active sessions,
      checkout, purchases, and client compatibility to the owner.
